## Project Overview

Designed for the **TEKNOFEST 2026 FPV Tracking Competition** as part of **Team AeroTrack (ID: 5345922)**. The drone is fully autonomous and operates entirely without GNSS in a GPS-denied environment. All heavy AI processing is offloaded to a Ground Control Station (GCS), keeping the airframe at just ~645g AUW — well within the 4kg / 15-inch limits.

**My Role: Software Integration & GCS**

---

## System Architecture

The system is split across three domains that communicate via RF links:

**Ground Control Station (GCS)**
Runs the full AI pipeline on Ubuntu 22.04 LTS via ROS 2 Humble:
- Walksnail Avatar V2 streams 1080p60 directly over USB (~40ms, no capture card needed)
- OpenCV pre-processes each frame: BGR conversion → 640×640 resize → channel normalization
- YOLOv11n runs at 60–90 FPS with a 0.45 confidence threshold to minimize miss-rates
- ByteTrack maintains target identity across temporary occlusions
- Kalman filter bridges target-loss gaps up to 100ms without IMU drift
- PPO policy maps observations to SET_ATTITUDE_TARGET commands
- MAVROS node injects commands to the drone via MAVLink

**RF Links**
- 2.4GHz ELRS for manual RC (pilot authority, hardware interrupt — bypasses ROS 2 entirely)
- 915MHz SiK MAVLink for autonomous attitude commands (~20ms RTT)
- Walksnail digital FPV via USB (direct to GCS GPU)

**Drone**
Executes only SET_ATTITUDE_TARGET (MAVLink #82) commands — no companion computer onboard.

---

## 95ms End-to-End Control Loop

| Stage | Latency | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| Walksnail digital link + USB | ~40ms | Replaces analog+capture (~88ms) |
| YOLOv11n GPU inference | ~30ms | 60–90 FPS on GTX 1660+ |
| Kalman update + PPO inference | ~5ms | CPU/GPU combined |
| MAVLink command (SiK 915MHz) | ~20ms | Bidirectional |
| **Total loop latency** | **≈95ms** | Kalman prediction compensates |

---

## My Contributions

### 1. Walksnail USB Video Pipeline
Documented and implemented the full video pipeline. The Walksnail Avatar V2 streams 1080p60 directly via USB to the GCS GPU — eliminating capture card latency (~88ms with analog) and bringing it down to ~40ms. OpenCV pre-processes each frame before YOLOv11n inference.

### 2. ROS 2 / MAVROS GCS Node (C++)
Integrated the custom ROS 2 node managing flight mode switching and attitude command injection. Three key engineering solutions were required:

- **Mode switch debouncing:** A 1-second cooldown timer prevents MAVROS from crashing due to rapid mode-switch request spamming
- **Raw integer mode mapping:** Bypasses MAVROS string-dictionary errors by commanding raw ArduCopter mode IDs (0, 2, 20) instead of strings like "GUIDED_NOGPS"
- **Asynchronous service calls:** Flight mode changes use async MAVROS clients to avoid blocking the main 50ms telemetry timer loop

### 3. Flight State Machine Design

| State | Mode | Trigger | Behavior |
|---|---|---|---|
| Manual Take-off | STABILIZE (0) | Pilot CH5 | Pilot positions drone in target zone |
| Target Lock-on | — | YOLO conf ≥ 0.45 | Operator confirms, ByteTrack initialises |
| Autonomous Tracking | GUIDED_NOGPS (20) | Pilot CH5 flip | MAVROS injects SET_ATTITUDE_TARGET @ ~95ms |
| Kalman Bridge | GUIDED_NOGPS (20) | Target lost ≤100ms | Kalman predicts position, PPO stays active |
| Sweep Scan | GUIDED_NOGPS (20) | Target lost >100ms | Steady yaw rotation for 360° re-acquisition |
| Failsafe | ALT_HOLD (2) | CH7 or scan timeout | Barometer hold, pilot resumes manually |

### 4. SITL Validation
Validated the full closed-loop pipeline using ArduPilot SITL with MAVROS 2.4+ on Ubuntu 22.04:
- Identified and resolved a race condition where MAVROS locks RC overrides if initialized before the ArduPilot physics engine — established a strict chronological boot protocol
- Confirmed successful GUIDED_NOGPS handoff with 95ms quaternion injection latency

